<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88017" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προμηθ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έος</span>, ὁ, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Προμᾱθεύς</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Prometheus,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐπιμηθεύς</span> (<u>Forethought</u>
			and Afterthought), <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				510
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				85
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				320d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHib.</u>
				1.27.85
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Προμαθέος
				Αἰδὼς [θυγάτηρ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				7.44
			</span></i>; =
			<i>Summanus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i>: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Προμηθεῖς, οἱ,</span> of workers in clay, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Prom.Es</u>
				2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Appellat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτὸν γάρ σε δεῖ προμηθέως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					86
				</span></i>
			: as Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προμᾱθεὺς ἀρχά</span>
			<i>provident</i> rule (prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προμᾱθίς</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				700
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> name for <i>unity,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theol.Ar.
				5
			</span></i>: for <i>nine,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				57
			</span></i>.</div>
